2. To check a five digits divided into two groups with spaces between them. Example: "123 45"
        - \d{3}\s\d{2} , ^\d{3}\s\d{2}$ (entire string to be postal code)
    
3. Write a regex that matches a date written according to the international standard ISO 8601
        - \d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}, ^\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}$ (only date and in same format)
        
